<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct private machinery orders up 44.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct private machinery orders up 44.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, rose a seasonally adjusted 44.2 percent in October from the previous month to 1.36 trillion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 OCT		SEPT</p>
<p> Overall	    +21.0		 +6.5</p>
<p> Private	    +44.2		-10.2</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 OCT		SEPT</p>
<p> Public	     +38.4		+16.3</p>
<p> External	   -20.4		+28.9</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 OCT		SEPT</p>
<p> Overall	    +27.4	     +11.7</p>
<p> Private	    +34.1		+3.6</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 OCT		 SEPT</p>
<p> Public	     +44.6		 +8.9</p>
<p> External	   -6.7		+30.3</p>
</text>
